WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.750
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.513
happening all the time, so we gathered

00:00:03.513 --> 00:00:05.430
some of the most-hyped
products from November

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.060
to test for ourselves.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.380
Let's start with the brand
everyone is talking about,

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.420
Ariana Grande's REM Beauty.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:12.550
I don't have every product,

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.110
but I have a decent batch.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.950
Now, I love miss ponytail,

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.700
and I will buy anything she tells me to,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.450
but we definitely have some products here

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.040
that are underwhelming.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.680
The skips for me are
the volumizing mascara

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.670
and the eyeliner.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.280
The mascara was pretty clumpy,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.220
and I've tried better mascara formulas

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.500
at the drugstore.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.053
The eyeliner also wasn't
great, which is shocking,

00:00:32.053 --> 00:00:34.010
because I feel like that's her thing.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.680
It was just skipping on the eye,

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.320
and it wasn't as intensely black

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.750
as I wanted it to be.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.460
Everything else I tried I loved.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.170
The lip products are very pigmented

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.650
and comfortable on the lips.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.010
The plumping gloss has this
really nice minty scent,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.090
and the lipstick smells like vanilla cake.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.160
I love it.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.900
Also, I know everyone hated the packaging,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.150
but come on, this lipstick is so cute.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.600
It looks like a little astronaut!

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.660
The liquid shadow was super easy to blend

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:57.940
and looked pretty on the eyes.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.130
I will say, I wish it was more sparkly.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.790
It looked a little dull for me.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.331
If you can only get one product

00:01:03.331 --> 00:01:04.260
from this brand, though,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.530
get the highlighter topper.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.160
It's more on the metallic side,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.480
but not glittery at all,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.560
and it looks amazing on the skin.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.270
I freaked out when I saw that ELF came out

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.800
with basically their own version

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.500
of the ABH Brow Freeze.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.300
I still love that fluffy,
laminated brow look,

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.590
so of course I had to get it

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.040
and compare the two.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.020
Mine did come super
cloudy and white-looking.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.720
On the website, the product
looks totally clear,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.170
just like the ABH Brow Freeze,

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.540
so I don't know what that's about.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.323
Anyway, I applied the ELF
Brow Lift on my right brow

00:01:33.323 --> 00:01:35.730
using the specific Brow Lift Applicator

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.452
they released with it, and already,

00:01:38.452 --> 00:01:41.302
I could tell that this is
the same as the Brow Freeze,

00:01:41.302 --> 00:01:43.290
or at least as close as you can get.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:44.580
It didn't take a lot of product

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.640
to get the brow looking full and fluffy,

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.330
and I also love the applicator,

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.180
because it came with this

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.138
little flat piece at the end

00:01:51.138 --> 00:01:53.490
to really press the brow hairs into place.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.610
I used the ABH Brow
Freeze on my left brow,

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.970
so you can see how similar the effect is.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.130
I highly, highly, highly recommend this

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:02.360
if you're into this kind of brow look.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.597
I was so confused when I saw this

00:02:04.597 --> 00:02:07.239
petri-dish-looking
highlighter all over TikTok.

00:02:07.239 --> 00:02:09.350
This is the Huda Beauty Rose Quartz

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.991
Face Gloss Highlighting
Dew, and it's essentially

00:02:11.991 --> 00:02:15.090
a cream highlighter-face gloss hybrid.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.400
I've never been interested
in these kinds of products,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.350
because they tend to remove foundation,

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.410
and that's pretty much
what happened with this.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.710
The formula is almost tacky.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.070
It's very sticky.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:26.360
So everywhere I applied it,

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.750
it was lifting off more
and more foundation.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.810
The glow it gives is actually pretty nice,

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.410
but it's not worth the trouble for me.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.780
I'd rather just use a powder highlighter.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.800
Purple blush has been everywhere lately,

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.280
and I've been wanting to try it so bad.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.450
This is one of the purple
blushes I kept seeing,

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:43.190
the Made by Mitchell Blursh.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:44.400
I'm not saying that weird,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.530
that's what it's called.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.960
I was playing with fire

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.290
applying a liquid blush

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:50.240
over my already powdered base,

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.360
a purple blush nonetheless,

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.470
but I did it anyway,

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.460
and this formula actually blew my mind.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.030
It didn't remove any foundation,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.270
it didn't get patchy,

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.750
and it was so effortless to blend out.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.690
I don't know if I'm super sold

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.020
on purple blush on my skin tone.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.660
I just don't think that
it's more flattering

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.040
than my normal peachy-orange blushes,

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.180
but it's still pretty.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.770
I definitely want more
blushes from this brand.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.750
I was so intrigued by this concealer,

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.480
because it's described
as a concealer serum,

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.300
which I've never tried before.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.860
When I was applying it with my brush,

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.040
I was getting excited

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.090
because it seemed like
the coverage was great.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.640
It was super creamy.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.800
But then I started blending.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.392
On the rest of my face,
it blended out just fine

00:03:30.392 --> 00:03:31.650
and I thought it looked good,

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:34.410
but something weird was
happening on my under-eyes,

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.470
specifically on my right side.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.010
The product started to pill up

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.540
and get kind of weird,

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.970
but it didn't do that on my left side,

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.010
so I'm confused.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.170
I think it all looked better

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.320
after I set it with
powder, finished my makeup,

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.840
and applied my setting spray.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.910
But I'm not a huge fan
of this concealer yet.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.180
Maybe I just have to try it again

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.560
with a different foundation.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.320
I am so not a glitter person,

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:54.420
but I saw some videos

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.220
of this particular glitter in action

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.350
and fell in love.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:00.580
This is the LA Girl
Glitterholic Glitter Topper

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:01.780
in Holo-Glam.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.090
Oh, my God, say that five times fast.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.020
It has this color-shifting magic in it

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.570
that makes it look like you
have nothing on your eyes,

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:09.890
but then you move your head

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.673
and it's, like, purple, and then blue.

00:04:11.673 --> 00:04:13.070
I don't even know how to describe it,

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:14.300
but I'm really obsessed.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.730
It has a built-in base,

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.180
so you don't need to use
any glitter adhesive.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.730
Just apply it with your fingers.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.170
I think I would still use
this with a glitter base

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.050
just for some extra security,

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:25.360
but I'm paranoid.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.631
I love this, and it's only 6 bucks.

